{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Silver or vessels to guard.</b> This is an unpaid bailee. For it is not customary to take a wage for guarding silver and vessels, because one takes no trouble in guarding them but simply places them in a safe place like the rest of his possessions; therefore if they were stolen or lost, he is exempt." "<b>And it is stolen from the house of the man.</b> This verse comes to exempt the one who steals after the thief." "<b>He shall pay double.</b> Since he claims the claim of a thief — i.e., he has admitted that the one who took it is a thief — therefore he pays as is the law of a thief: he shall pay double to his fellow. But another verse says: ושלם אותו בראשו וחמשיתו יוסף עליו. How can both these verses stand? Rather: whoever pays principal pays a fifth, and one who does not pay principal is exempt from the fifth."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:59:42.788095720Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}